# AWS training

The AWS end-to-end tier runs the shared model lifecycle on Fargate. Implement the
project-specific adapters in `src/{{ package_name }}/pipeline/project_factory.py`.
Classification and forecasting use the same contracts with task-specific serving bundles.
The default adapter deliberately raises `NotImplementedError` until implemented.

## Shared cloud lifecycle

Follow [AWS deployment](aws-deployment.md), then [AWS lifecycle](aws-lifecycle.md).
The task definition now starts `{{ package_name }}.aws.lifecycle` with command `train`.
It reads the normal S3 project paths and uses a shared remote MLflow registry.
Do not assume that uploading data under an old isolated-job prefix changes those paths.

```bash
gh workflow run lifecycle-aws.yml --ref main -f environment=dev -f operation=train
```

Review logs, evaluation, the promotion decision and the active serving release.
A successful task can legitimately skip promotion if the challenger fails the policy.
When serving is enabled, promotion refreshes ECS and verifies the loaded release.
Image rollbacks and model rollbacks are separate operations.

## Optional isolated training utility

The earlier isolated training utility remains available for adapter development:

```bash
uv run --extra aws python -m {{ package_name }}.aws.train --help
uv run --extra aws python -m {{ package_name }}.aws.fargate_train --help
```

`aws.train` runs locally with explicit input/work/model/output directories and a
job-local tracking backend. It exports a reloadable candidate; it does not promote
the shared champion. `aws.fargate_train` wraps that utility with S3 transport when
explicitly invoked. It is no longer the default ECS task entry point.

Build and test the isolated adapter image after implementing the adapters:

```bash
uv sync --extra aws
docker build -f Dockerfile.training -t {{ project_slug }}-training:local .
uv run --extra aws python scripts/training_container_smoke_test.py \
  --image {{ project_slug }}-training:local
```

The container smoke fixture supplies synthetic adapters; it does not verify your
production dataset or project training implementation. SageMaker request helpers
remain optional and cloud execution has not been verified.

## Verification scope and cleanup

The forecasting reference project was verified on AWS, including registry,
persistence and a technical identical-weight release switch/rollback. Generated
projects still require account-specific IAM, KMS, networking and adapter verification.
Offline tests cannot establish cloud deployment success.

Use [AWS deployment](aws-deployment.md) for cleanup. Preserve models/metadata that
matter before removing the stack, and check retained snapshots, S3 versions, ECR,
secret recovery windows and the separate Terraform state bucket.
